{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and accepted at the `mitigation` stage.\n\n**Root cause:** The `memory-limit-quota` ResourceQuota (1Gi memory) rejects any pod that doesn't declare a memory request or limit. The `search` deployment only set CPU, so its ReplicaSet could not create pods and the service had no running replicas.\n\n**Fix:** Added a memory request of `128Mi` and a limit of `256Mi` to the `search` deployment in `hotel-reservation`. The rollout succeeded, the pod is Running and registered in Consul, and all pods in the namespace are Running. The quota is unchanged (128Mi of 1Gi used).\n\nI did not check end-user latency after submitting, so whether it has fully recovered is still unconfirmed. The other services also declare only CPU, which would hit the same quota error if they are ever recreated."}}
